hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1740","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Ubaydullah ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi, from Umm Salamah daughter of Abi Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When we descended in the land of Abyssinia, we neighbored therein the best neighbor, an-Najashi; we were secure upon our religion and worshipped Allah, not harmed, nor hearing anything we disliked. When that reached Quraysh, they resolved to send to an-Najashi regarding us two strong men, and to gift to an-Najashi gifts of what is deemed rare of the goods of Makkah, and among what was most pleasing coming to him from it was leather; so they gathered for him much leather, and left none of his patricians without gifting him a gift. Then they sent that with Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi and Amr ibn al-As ibn Wail as-Sahmi, and gave them their instructions, and said to them: Give to each patrician his gift before you speak to an-Najashi regarding them, then present to an-Najashi his gifts, then ask him to hand them to you before he speaks to them. She said: They set out and came to an-Najashi while we were with him in the best abode and with the best neighbor. There remained none of his patricians without they gave him his gift before speaking to an-Najashi. Then they said to each patrician of them: There have inclined to the land of the king from us foolish youths who parted from the religion of their people and did not enter into your religion, and came with an invented religion which neither we nor you know. The nobles of their people have sent us to the king regarding them to return them to them. When we speak to the king regarding them, advise him to hand them to us and not speak to them, for their people have greater insight into them and know better what they faulted them for. They said to them: Yes. Then they presented their gifts to an-Najashi and he accepted them from them. Then they spoke to him and said to him: O king, there have inclined to your land from us foolish youths who parted from the religion of their people and did not enter into your religion, and came with an invented religion which neither we nor you know. The nobles of their people, of their fathers and uncles and kinsfolk, have sent us to you regarding them to return them to them, for they have greater insight into them and know better what they faulted them for and reproached them in. She said: Nothing was more hateful to Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah and Amr ibn al-As than that an-Najashi should hear their speech. His patricians around him said: They have spoken truth, O king; their people have greater insight into them and know better what they faulted them for, so hand them to them to return them to their lands and people. He said: an-Najashi became angry, then said: No, by Allah, by Allah, then I shall not hand them to them nor oppress a people who neighbored me and descended in my lands and chose me over others besides me, until I call them and ask them what these two say regarding their affair. If they are as they say, I shall hand them to them and return them to their people; and if they are upon other than that, I shall protect them from them and make good their neighborhood as long as they neighbor me. She said: Then he sent to the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and called them. When his messenger came to them, they gathered, then some said to others: What will you say to the man when you come to him? They said: By Allah, we shall say what our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught us and commanded us with, whatever happens therein. When they came to him, and an-Najashi had called his bishops and they spread their scriptures around him, he asked them and said: What is this religion by which you parted from your people and did not enter into my religion nor into the religion of any of these nations? She said: The one who spoke to him was Jafar ibn Abi Talib, and he said to him: O king, we were a people of ignorance, worshipping idols, eating carrion, committing shameful deeds, severing kinship, treating neighbors badly, the strong of us eating the weak. We were upon that until Allah sent to us a messenger from us whose lineage and truthfulness and trustworthiness and chastity we know. He called us to Allah to declare Him One and worship Him, and cast off what we and our fathers used to worship besides Him of stones and idols. He commanded us with truthfulness of speech, fulfillment of trust, joining kinship, good neighborhood, refraining from forbidden things and blood. He forbade us from shameful deeds, false speech, eating the wealth of the orphan, and accusing chaste women. He commanded us to worship Allah alone, not associating anything with Him, and commanded us with prayer and zakah and fasting. He said: He enumerated to him the matters of Islam. We believed him and believed in him and followed him upon what he came with. We worshipped Allah alone and did not associate anything with Him, and forbade what He forbade us and permitted what He permitted us. Our people turned upon us and tortured us and tempted us from our religion to return us to worshipping idols from worshipping Allah, and to deem lawful what we used to deem lawful of evil things. When they overpowered us and wronged us and were harsh upon us and stood between us and our religion, we went out to your land and chose you over others besides you, and desired your neighborhood, and hoped that we would not be wronged with you, O king. She said: an-Najashi said to him: Have you with you of what he came with from Allah anything? She said: Jafar said to him: Yes. an-Najashi said to him: Recite it to me. He recited to him the beginning of Kaf-Ha-Ya-Ayn-Sad. She said: By Allah, an-Najashi wept until he moistened his beard, and his bishops wept until they moistened their scriptures when they heard what was recited to them. Then an-Najashi said: Indeed this, by Allah, and what Musa came with, come from one niche. Go forth, for by Allah I shall never hand them to you, nor oppress them. Umm Salamah said: When they went out from him, Amr ibn al-As said: By Allah, I shall inform them tomorrow of their fault with him, then uproot by it their remnant. She said: Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah, and he was the more God-fearing of the two men among us, said to him: Do not do it, for they have kinship, even if they opposed us. He said: By Allah, I shall inform him that they claim that Isa son of Maryam is a servant. She said: Then he went to him in the morning and said to him: O king, they say regarding Isa son of Maryam a grave saying, so send to them and ask them what they say regarding him. She said: He sent to them asking them about him. She said: Nothing like it had befallen us. The people gathered and some said to others: What will you say regarding Isa when he asks you about him? They said: By Allah, we shall say regarding him what Allah said and what our Prophet came with, whatever happens therein. When they entered upon him he said to them: What do you say regarding Isa son of Maryam? Jafar ibn Abi Talib said to him: We say regarding him what our Prophet came with: He is the servant of Allah and His messenger and His spirit and His word which He cast to Maryam, the virgin, the chaste. She said: an-Najashi struck his hand to the ground and took from it a stick, then said: Isa son of Maryam did not exceed what you said by this stick. His patricians snorted around him when he said what he said. He said: Even if you snort, by Allah. Go, for you are secure in my land, and as-suyum are the secure; whoever insults you shall be fined, then whoever insults you shall be fined. I would not wish to have a mountain of gold and that I harmed a man of you. Ad-dabr in the tongue of Abyssinia is the mountain. Return to them their gifts, for we have no need of them. By Allah, Allah did not take bribery from me when He returned my kingdom to me that I should take bribery in it, nor did people obey me in it that I should obey them in it. She said: They went out from him disgraced, with what they came with returned to them, and we remained with him in the best abode with the best neighbor. She said: By Allah, while we were upon that, there descended upon him, meaning one who disputed him in his kingdom. She said: By Allah, we never knew grief more severe than the grief we grieved at that, fearing that he would prevail over an-Najashi and there would come a man who does not know of our right what an-Najashi knew of it. She said: an-Najashi marched, and between them was the breadth of the Nile. She said: The companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Who is a man who will go out until he attends the encounter of the people then bring us the news? She said: az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam said: I. She said: And he was among the youngest of the people in age. She said: They inflated a waterskin for him and he placed it upon his chest, then swam upon it until he went out to the side of the Nile where the meeting of the people was, then set out until he attended them. She said: We supplicated Allah for an-Najashi for victory over his enemy and establishment for him in his lands, and the affair of Abyssinia became settled for him. We were with him in the best dwelling until we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in Makkah."
"22865","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abdullah ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham al-Makhzumi, from Umm Salamah daughter of Abi Umayyah ibn al-Mughirah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: When we descended the land of Abyssinia, we neighbored in it the best neighbor, an-Najashi; he secured us in our religion, and we worshipped Allah, exalted, not harmed and not hearing anything we disliked. So when that reached Quraysh, they resolved to send to an-Najashi concerning us two strong men, and to gift an-Najashi gifts of what was deemed choice of the goods of Mecca, and of the most wondrous that would come to him of it was leather. So they gathered for him much leather, and did not leave any of his patricians without gifting him a gift. Then they sent with that Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi and Amr ibn al-As ibn Wail as-Sahmi, and ordered them their affair, and said to them: Give to every patrician his gift before you speak to an-Najashi concerning them, then present to an-Najashi his gifts, then ask him to surrender them to you before he speaks to them. She said: So they went out and came to an-Najashi, while we were with him in the best abode and best neighborhood. So no patrician of his patricians remained except they gave him his gift before they spoke to an-Najashi. Then they said to every patrician of them: Indeed there have inclined to the land of the king from us foolish youths; they left the religion of their people and did not enter into your religion, and came with an invented religion we do not know, neither we nor you. And the nobles of their people have sent us to the king concerning them to return them to them. So when we speak to the king concerning them, advise him to surrender them to us and not speak to them, for indeed their people have more insight into them and know better what they faulted them for. So they said to them: Yes. Then they brought their gifts near to an-Najashi, and he accepted them from them. Then they spoke to him and said to him: O king, indeed there have inclined to your land from us foolish youths; they left the religion of their people and did not enter into your religion, and came with an invented religion we do not know, neither we nor you. And the nobles of their people, of their fathers and uncles and kinsmen, have sent us to you concerning them to return them to them, for they have more insight into them and know better what they faulted them for and blamed them for in it. She said: And nothing was more hateful to Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah and Amr ibn al-As than that an-Najashi hear their speech. So his patricians around him said: They spoke truth, O king; their people have more insight into them and know better what they faulted them for, so surrender them to them and let them return them to their lands and their people. She said: So an-Najashi became angry, then said: No, by Allah, then, I will not surrender them to them, nor wrong a people who neighbored me and descended my lands and chose me over others, until I call them and ask them what these two say about their affair. If they are as they say, I will surrender them to them and return them to their people, and if they are upon other than that, I will protect them from them and do good to neighbor them so long as they neighbor me. She said: Then he sent to the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and called them. So when his messenger came to them, they gathered. Then some of them said to others: What will you say to the man when you come to him? They said: By Allah, we will say what we know and what our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us with, whatever happens in that. So when they came to him, and an-Najashi had called his bishops, and they spread their scriptures around him, to ask them, he said: What is this religion by which you left your people and did not enter into my religion nor into the religion of anyone of these nations? She said: So the one who spoke to him was Jafar ibn Abi Talib, and he said to him: O king, we were a people of ignorance; we worshipped idols, ate carrion, committed immoralities, severed kinship, did evil to neighbors, the strong of us eating the weak. So we were upon that until Allah sent to us a messenger from us; we know his lineage and his truthfulness and his trustworthiness and his chastity. So he called us to Allah, exalted, to declare Him one and worship Him, and cast off what we and our fathers used to worship besides Him of stones and idols. And he commanded truthful speech, fulfillment of trust, joining kinship, good neighboring, refraining from prohibitions and blood, and forbade us immoralities and false speech and eating the wealth of the orphan and slandering chaste women. And he commanded us to worship Allah alone, not associating anything with Him, and commanded us with prayer and zakah and fasting. He said: So he enumerated to him the matters of Islam. So we believed him and believed in him and followed him upon what he came with. So we worshipped Allah alone and did not associate anything with Him, and forbade what he forbade us, and permitted what he permitted us. So our people transgressed against us, so they tortured us, so they tried us from our religion to return us to worshipping idols from worshipping Allah, and that we permit what we used to permit of foul things. And when they overpowered us and wronged us and burdened us and stood between us and our religion, we went out to your land, and chose you over others, and desired your neighborhood, and hoped that we would not be wronged with you, O king. She said: So an-Najashi said to him: Is there with you of what he brought from Allah anything? She said: So Jafar said to him: Yes. So an-Najashi said to him: So recite it to me. So he recited to him the opening of Kaf-Ha-Ya-Ayn-Sad. She said: So by Allah, an-Najashi wept until he moistened his beard, and his bishops wept until they moistened their scriptures when they heard what was recited to them. Then an-Najashi said: Indeed this and what Musa came with come from one niche. Go, for by Allah, I will never surrender them to you, nor wrong them. Umm Salamah, may Allah be pleased with her, said: So when they went out from him, Amr ibn al-As said: By Allah, I will come to him tomorrow faulting them to him, then I will uproot their green with him. She said: So Abdullah ibn Abi Rabiah said to him, and he was the more God-fearing of the two men among us: Do not do, for indeed they have kinship, even if they opposed us. He said: By Allah, I will inform him that they claim that Isa son of Maryam, peace be upon them, is a servant. She said: Then he came to him in the morning and said to him: O king, indeed they say about Isa son of Maryam a grave saying, so send to them and ask them about what they say about him. Umm Salamah said: So he sent to them asking them about him. She said: And nothing like it had befallen us. So the people gathered, and some of them said to others: What will you say about Isa when he asks you about him? They said: By Allah, we will say about him what Allah, glorified and exalted, said and what our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came with, whatever happens in that. So when they entered upon him, he said to them: What do you say about Isa son of Maryam? So Jafar ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: We say about him what our Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came with: He is the servant of Allah and His Messenger and His spirit and His word which He cast to Maryam the virgin the chaste. She said: So an-Najashi struck his hand upon the ground and took from it a stick, then said: Isa son of Maryam did not exceed what you said by this stick. So his patricians snorted around him when he said what he said. So he said: Even if you snort, by Allah. Go, for you are safe in my land, and as-suyum are the secure; whoever insults you is fined, then whoever insults you is fined, then whoever insults you is fined. I would not love that I have a mountain of gold and that I harmed a man of you, and ad-dabr in the tongue of Abyssinia is the mountain. Return to them their gifts, for we have no need of them. For by Allah, Allah did not take a bribe from me when He returned my kingdom to me that I take a bribe in it, and people did not obey me in it that I obey them in it. She said: So they went out from him disgraced, with what they came with returned to them, and we stayed with him in the best abode with the best neighbor. She said: By Allah, while we were upon that, there descended upon him one disputing him in his kingdom. She said: By Allah, we never knew grief at all more severe than grief we grieved at that, fearing that would prevail over an-Najashi, so a man would come who does not know of our right what an-Najashi knew of it. She said: And an-Najashi marched, and between them was the width of the Nile. He said: So the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Which man will go out until he attends the battle of the people, then brings us the news? She said: So az-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I. She said: And he was of the youngest of the people in age. She said: So they inflated for him a waterskin and he placed it on his chest, then swam upon it until he went out to the side of the Nile where the meeting of the people was, then went until he attended them. She said: And we supplicated Allah, exalted, for an-Najashi for victory over his enemy and establishment for him in his lands. And the affair of Abyssinia became firm upon him, so we were with him in the best dwelling until we came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was in Mecca."
